WEBVTT

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.994
" Namsac"

00:00:31.997 --> 00:00:35.751
" Episode 5 "

00:00:40.798 --> 00:00:42.716
Amazing.

00:00:46.387 --> 00:00:47.304
Hey, pay attention.

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:48.681
Watch where you 're goin '.

00:00:48.889 --> 00:00:50.599
Oh, l 'm sorry.

00:00:52.393 --> 00:00:53.352
C' mere.

00:00:53.561 --> 00:00:55.229
U-Um, um...!

00:00:55.437 --> 00:00:56.605
Somebody!

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:01.902
L-l 'm sorry for bumping into you.
But that was beyond my control.

00:01:02.111 --> 00:01:03.404
L-Let's be calm about--

00:01:04.572 --> 00:01:08.993
Shut up! lf you cause trouble for someone,
the thing to do is pay up.

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:12.621
M-Money? <i>Well...</i> l don 't have much on <i>me.</i>

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.999
Then l 'll take that camera. And the watch.

00:01:15.207 --> 00:01:17.835
N-Not the camera! l need it for my job!

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:20.129
As if l care!

00:01:20.337 --> 00:01:22.298
C-Come on! Please!

00:01:22.506 --> 00:01:24.341
Leave him alone, Dao.

00:01:25.259 --> 00:01:27.678
What're you doing to the tourist?

00:01:27.886 --> 00:01:29.138
Nami, huh?

00:01:29.346 --> 00:01:32.308
This city's reputation will get worse and worse.

00:01:32.516 --> 00:01:34.893
So what if it does?! Get lost!

00:01:35.102 --> 00:01:36.937
You just don 't listen to reason.

00:01:38.981 --> 00:01:39.690
Hey, seriously?

00:01:39.898 --> 00:01:44.320
I won 't kill you. l 'll let you off
with some holes in your limbs.

00:01:44.528 --> 00:01:47.531
You 're gonna stick up for
this stranger and <i>shoot</i> me?!

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.201
That's not all. l 'll tell the
mama-<i>san</i> at Molina about this.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.829
You don 't want to get banned
from that joint, do you?

00:01:56.165 --> 00:01:58.250
There, that's more like it.

00:01:58.459 --> 00:02:00.002
You better be ready later!

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.963
You mean the match? Bring it on!

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:07.676
That worked out somehow.

00:02:07.885 --> 00:02:09.428
Th-Thank you.

00:02:09.637 --> 00:02:11.221
But that...

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.057
Oh, this gun?

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:14.600
It's broken.

00:02:16.268 --> 00:02:17.811
What's the big idea?!

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:18.854
Did l scare you?

00:02:19.063 --> 00:02:23.651
Of course you did! l mean,
l 'm grateful you helped <i>me...</i>

00:02:27.363 --> 00:02:30.199
And for that, you owe me $5,000.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.703
--Pay up.
--Huh?!

00:02:36.914 --> 00:02:38.374
That's cheap, right?

00:02:38.582 --> 00:02:42.002
That guy Dao back there
is famous for his brutality!

00:02:42.211 --> 00:02:45.214
If you had tried anything,
you could have wound up dead.

00:02:45.422 --> 00:02:45.881
Is that so?

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:48.634
Be grateful for my kindness!

00:02:48.842 --> 00:02:52.137
Then while you' re being kind,
l 'd like you to leave me alone.

00:02:52.346 --> 00:02:55.849
I can 't do that. l felt like
l was in danger, too! And so--

00:02:56.058 --> 00:02:57.726
And so, $5,000?

00:02:57.935 --> 00:03:00.646
In this city, you could live in luxury
for a year with that amount.

00:03:00.854 --> 00:03:02.439
Of course l don 't have that much money.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:03.982
Then let me have this camera.

00:03:04.191 --> 00:03:06.610
Get real! l need this for my job.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:10.781
Por your job? So what is your job, anyway?

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:13.992
I 'm a struggling photographer.

00:03:14.201 --> 00:03:15.160
A photographer!

00:03:15.369 --> 00:03:16.412
Wh-What gives?

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.082
Then you must be here to cover that, too.

00:03:52.322 --> 00:03:55.033
The winner! Bloody Oueen!

00:04:00.414 --> 00:04:02.207
Dear me, that's violent.

00:04:02.416 --> 00:04:04.168
But it packs a real punch, huh?

00:04:04.376 --> 00:04:05.252
I guess.

00:04:05.461 --> 00:04:08.338
We take ASes that were
decommissioned after conflicts ended,

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:10.299
and people bet on them
in pro wrestling matches.

00:04:10.507 --> 00:04:12.551
It's become big business in this city.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:15.471
Those robots... ASes, you said?

00:04:15.679 --> 00:04:18.932
I 'm surprised the police allow it.
Aren 't those military weapons?

00:04:19.141 --> 00:04:21.769
It all comes down to money in this town.

00:04:21.977 --> 00:04:25.022
Makes sense. Looks like
business is booming, too.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.902
See? lf you get the scoop on this,
you 're guaranteed a Peanut Prize!

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:32.988
So come on, $5,000.

00:04:33.197 --> 00:04:36.158
I told you, no way.
Also, it's called a Pulitzer Prize.

00:04:36.366 --> 00:04:38.660
It's the only place like this in the world!

00:04:38.869 --> 00:04:40.829
There are so many different ASes <i>here.</i>

00:04:41.038 --> 00:04:44.416
Savages, Bushnells,
and M istrals, and also Cyclones!

00:04:44.625 --> 00:04:46.126
Y-You really know this stuff.

00:04:46.335 --> 00:04:50.923
Well, yeah! l 'm the owner of
one of the competing teams.

00:04:51.131 --> 00:04:53.967
I have a first-rate AS and a team.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:02.643
Good for you.

00:05:02.851 --> 00:05:05.646
What's with that reaction?
l bet you don 't believe me!

00:05:05.854 --> 00:05:08.941
You bet right. There's no way
a girl who tries to get money

00:05:09.149 --> 00:05:12.653
out of a guy like me on a street
corner has a robot like that.

00:05:12.861 --> 00:05:16.031
I do so have one! l need money for parts!

00:05:16.240 --> 00:05:17.241
Also, two hours.

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:18.325
Huh?

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:19.743
Come with me!

00:05:27.668 --> 00:05:30.128
Well? High-quality, huh?

00:05:30.337 --> 00:05:33.006
This... is high-quality?

00:05:34.383 --> 00:05:34.925
Shit!

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.094
Riley! What're you doing?!

00:05:37.302 --> 00:05:40.389
I can 't help it!
l 'm a heavy machinery mechanic!

00:05:40.597 --> 00:05:43.559
Oil pressure is oil pressure, right?
Pigure something out.

00:05:43.767 --> 00:05:44.893
Wonderful...

00:05:45.102 --> 00:05:46.228
lt's awful.

00:05:46.436 --> 00:05:48.272
Sure, it's broken here and there,

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.774
but it' ll be fine once we buy some parts.

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:52.276
That just leaves money!

00:05:52.484 --> 00:05:53.318
Hey, Nami!

00:05:53.527 --> 00:05:55.112
What, Asch?

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:57.781
Sure enough, we need
two #50 muscle packages

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:00.951
and an intervertebral disk damper.
How's the money situation?

00:06:01.159 --> 00:06:02.494
It's all right.

00:06:02.703 --> 00:06:04.830
Um... Come to think of it,
what's your name?

00:06:05.038 --> 00:06:05.497
Lemon.

00:06:05.706 --> 00:06:07.916
Mr. Lemon here is going to cover it.

00:06:08.125 --> 00:06:08.709
Hey!

00:06:08.917 --> 00:06:10.836
Cool. Well the sooner the better.

00:06:11.044 --> 00:06:13.589
Don 't say that! lt's not as if l <i>agreed...</i>

00:06:13.797 --> 00:06:15.924
Just make it a loan! Please!

00:06:16.133 --> 00:06:20.429
If we win tonight's match,
l can pay you back $5,000 in no time!

00:06:20.637 --> 00:06:22.848
With this heap? lmpossible.

00:06:23.056 --> 00:06:27.394
S-Sure, the mech 's not perfect,
but the operator's top-notch!

00:06:27.603 --> 00:06:29.062
--Oh?
--His name is Rick.

00:06:29.271 --> 00:06:31.106
They call him the Jungle Warbird.

00:06:31.315 --> 00:06:33.525
He's a former US Marine Corps ace--

00:06:33.734 --> 00:06:37.070
A big-time veteran who's crushed
more than ten opponents!

00:06:37.279 --> 00:06:39.698
--I have my doubts.
--You 'll <i>see</i> once you meet him.

00:06:39.907 --> 00:06:41.491
Wait, where <i>is</i> Rick?

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:45.078
Got me. Not too long ago,
he was getting himself dead drunk.

00:06:47.331 --> 00:06:48.665
Nami, there's trouble!

00:06:48.874 --> 00:06:50.542
Kaew, what's wrong?

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:55.172
It's Rick...

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:06.516
Rick was a horrible guy in lots of ways,

00:07:06.725 --> 00:07:09.227
but he didn 't deserve to be murdered.

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:12.689
Where are you going?

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.066
We've got a match.

00:07:14.274 --> 00:07:16.568
But wasn 't he your operator?

00:07:16.777 --> 00:07:19.529
That's right. l 'll do it instead.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:20.572
Do you have any experience?

00:07:20.781 --> 00:07:22.574
I can move it around, at least.

00:07:22.783 --> 00:07:24.534
Hey, Nami!

00:07:25.869 --> 00:07:29.331
I heard Rick got stabbed to death.

00:07:29.539 --> 00:07:32.167
Rough town, this! Scary, scary.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.586
Dao!

00:07:34.795 --> 00:07:38.090
I told you, you better be ready.

00:07:38.298 --> 00:07:41.843
I never could stand that American.

00:07:42.052 --> 00:07:44.554
Always braggin ' his head off.

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:46.139
You low-life creep!

00:07:46.348 --> 00:07:50.227
Well, wasn't it his everyday
behavior that's to blame?

00:07:53.939 --> 00:07:56.608
Hey. Don 't tell me you ' re going up against...

00:07:56.817 --> 00:08:00.445
That's right. Dao's team.
They have a pretty good mech, too.

00:08:00.654 --> 00:08:03.824
Let it go. That guy's not right!
l bet you ' ll get killed, too!

00:08:04.032 --> 00:08:05.617
I can 't do that!

00:08:09.496 --> 00:08:13.458
We've got to win and
make some money. We <i>have</i> to win!

00:08:13.667 --> 00:08:15.252
Otherwise...

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:17.754
Hey!

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:22.009
Sorry to bother you, Mr. Lemon.
l don 't need the $5,000 anymore.

00:08:22.217 --> 00:08:24.720
Hold on now. You must be getting desperate.

00:08:24.928 --> 00:08:26.346
--Maybe.
--This is crazy.

00:08:26.555 --> 00:08:28.181
I 'm fully aware of that.

00:08:30.475 --> 00:08:31.685
Well?

00:08:33.103 --> 00:08:33.979
Lovely...

00:08:34.187 --> 00:08:36.064
We' re boxed <i>in...</i>

00:08:36.273 --> 00:08:37.774
ls Rick here?

00:08:40.736 --> 00:08:41.945
What?

00:08:42.154 --> 00:08:43.780
Rick.

00:08:43.989 --> 00:08:45.866
He's an old acquaintance.

00:08:47.325 --> 00:08:49.578
He died. Just now.

00:08:49.786 --> 00:08:52.164
He got stabbed from behind.

00:08:52.372 --> 00:08:57.335
I <i>see.</i> l would always get on
his case about watching his back.

00:08:57.544 --> 00:08:58.503
That's too bad.

00:08:58.712 --> 00:09:00.464
Um, who are you?

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:04.968
A war buddy of his. We fought
together about three years ago.

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.554
I came because l heard
he'd become a competitor <i>here.</i>

00:09:07.763 --> 00:09:11.475
Too bad for you. Like l said,
he's dead. Now take a hike.

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:13.143
I hope to be a competitor, too.

00:09:13.351 --> 00:09:14.478
Huh?

00:09:14.686 --> 00:09:16.605
I want to be a competitor in this arena.

00:09:16.813 --> 00:09:18.982
I feel bad for Rick,
but the timing works out well.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.526
Would you be willing to hire me?

00:09:21.735 --> 00:09:25.447
You? You can operate an AS?

00:09:25.655 --> 00:09:26.490
A little.

00:09:26.698 --> 00:09:28.492
"A little. "

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.411
Idiots like you are a dime a dozen.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:34.122
This here is specialized
military equipment.

00:09:34.331 --> 00:09:37.084
It's not something some
ordinary guy can handle.

00:09:37.292 --> 00:09:40.170
You got that? lf so, then get lost.

00:09:40.378 --> 00:09:42.631
Are you listening?!

00:09:42.839 --> 00:09:44.716
Hey, don 't touch that!

00:09:44.925 --> 00:09:46.593
I 'm telling you to stop!

00:09:46.802 --> 00:09:48.470
You 're going to enter this mech in a match?

00:09:48.678 --> 00:09:50.097
Yeah, so what?

00:09:50.305 --> 00:09:52.349
It's just that it won 't be easy.

00:09:52.557 --> 00:09:54.601
Rick would have had trouble,
with his skills.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:58.480
Okay, M ister Expert,
what do you know about this mech?

00:09:58.688 --> 00:10:00.524
This mech?

00:10:00.732 --> 00:10:03.944
This is an early RK-91 .

00:10:04.152 --> 00:10:06.154
It doesn 't use a gas turbine,

00:10:06.363 --> 00:10:08.448
so it's inferior both in terms of
weight and output to the 92,

00:10:08.657 --> 00:10:10.742
which subsequently
became the standard.

00:10:10.951 --> 00:10:14.204
But that only applies to
the <i>extreme</i> limits of combat mobility.

00:10:14.412 --> 00:10:15.997
The torque control has some quirks,

00:10:16.206 --> 00:10:19.292
but an operator's skill
can compensate for those.

00:10:20.794 --> 00:10:23.797
In this mech 's case,
the problem is the cooling system.

00:10:24.005 --> 00:10:27.259
Prom what l can see,
you 're using the genuine model.

00:10:27.467 --> 00:10:28.593
Don 't bother.

00:10:28.802 --> 00:10:30.595
It's often said easy-to-obtain
exported cooler units

00:10:30.804 --> 00:10:32.556
aren't very compatible,
but there's no problem using one

00:10:32.764 --> 00:10:35.725
for just ten minutes,
and it's far less expensive.

00:10:35.934 --> 00:10:39.271
It'd be better to instead spend
that money on new muscle packages.

00:10:39.479 --> 00:10:44.568
Don 't talk like a know-it-all.
This mech is precious to us!

00:10:44.776 --> 00:10:47.696
Of course. You've worked hard to maintain it.

00:10:47.904 --> 00:10:50.240
It's the first model l ever used.

00:10:50.448 --> 00:10:53.618
I 'm surprised to find one
that's still functional.

00:10:55.328 --> 00:10:59.416
That's BS. You 're probably some
amateur who memorized all that.

00:10:59.624 --> 00:11:02.794
I 'm not an amateur. l 'm a specialist.

00:11:04.337 --> 00:11:06.965
Hey, Nami. What do we do?

00:11:07.174 --> 00:11:10.468
We' re out of time.
Maybe we should just let him try it.

00:11:19.811 --> 00:11:22.647
Why not?! There's no better option!

00:11:22.856 --> 00:11:24.983
If you want to do it, do it!

00:11:25.192 --> 00:11:25.859
Pair enough.

00:11:26.067 --> 00:11:28.445
What do we do about money, though?

00:11:28.653 --> 00:11:31.615
Without parts, this thing
can 't even stand up.

00:11:31.823 --> 00:11:35.577
Oh, about that. l can arrange up to $3,000.

00:11:35.785 --> 00:11:37.746
That's my card 's credit limit.

00:11:39.331 --> 00:11:41.166
I 'm kind of interested now.

00:11:41.374 --> 00:11:43.168
Thanks, mister!

00:11:46.004 --> 00:11:49.549
I figured maybe a longshot bet
like this could be fun.

00:11:49.758 --> 00:11:51.676
No, the odds are good.

00:11:51.885 --> 00:11:53.386
R-Really?

00:11:53.595 --> 00:11:55.222
By the way, what's your name?

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.098
It's Sousuke Sagara.

00:11:59.226 --> 00:12:02.187
I 've come to this city in search of something.

00:12:06.399 --> 00:12:07.400
We bought them!

00:12:07.609 --> 00:12:09.361
Good! Bring 'em over!

00:12:19.287 --> 00:12:20.830
I 'm done <i>here.</i>

00:12:23.375 --> 00:12:26.544
That's an unusual operator suit.
Can you really win?

00:12:26.753 --> 00:12:28.004
I intend to.

00:12:28.213 --> 00:12:29.881
Your opponent's strong.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:32.676
Not to mention brutal and cruel.

00:12:34.928 --> 00:12:36.388
That's good work.

00:12:37.806 --> 00:12:39.599
All right, l ' ll be back.

00:12:55.782 --> 00:12:57.284
W-Will he be okay?

00:12:57.492 --> 00:13:00.287
Who knows? But maybe
he' ll be unexpectedly good.

00:13:00.495 --> 00:13:01.579
Based on what?

00:13:02.497 --> 00:13:06.126
His build. You <i>see</i> it a lot with AS pilots.

00:13:06.334 --> 00:13:08.795
And the skin on his elbows
and wrists seemed thick.

00:13:09.004 --> 00:13:11.589
His knowledge was, well, pro-level.

00:13:13.174 --> 00:13:16.970
He might really be an ace.

00:13:24.769 --> 00:13:26.021
I figured out the quirk.

00:13:26.229 --> 00:13:28.982
Oh, sure. Do your best.

00:13:34.863 --> 00:13:37.574
Next bout, category: Bare Hands.

00:13:37.782 --> 00:13:42.203
Ogre! Operator, Ouang Van Dao!

00:13:42.412 --> 00:13:43.371
Versus!

00:13:43.580 --> 00:13:49.461
Crossbow! Operator, Sohsky Seagull!

00:13:49.669 --> 00:13:51.796
Crossbow? That heap?

00:13:52.005 --> 00:13:54.215
That's right. Cool, isn't it?

00:13:55.759 --> 00:13:59.179
It's a good name.
But it's certainly no Arbalest.

00:13:59.387 --> 00:14:01.139
Arba... lest?

00:14:01.348 --> 00:14:03.391
It was a crossbow used in siege warfare.

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.185
Huh...

00:14:08.563 --> 00:14:12.859
Kill! Kill! Kill! Kill!

00:14:15.737 --> 00:14:19.240
You 've got guts, pal!
l don 't know who you are in there,

00:14:19.449 --> 00:14:21.868
but it's too late to beg for your life!

00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:29.167
Pight!

00:14:32.379 --> 00:14:34.422
Drop dead!

00:14:58.029 --> 00:15:00.657
The winner, Crossbow!

00:15:04.202 --> 00:15:06.413
Wh-What happened?

00:15:06.621 --> 00:15:09.040
Dao passed out.

00:15:09.249 --> 00:15:11.334
When an AS rotates that much,

00:15:11.543 --> 00:15:15.213
not even its shock absorption system
can protect the operator.

00:15:15.422 --> 00:15:19.008
You could say it's like
being in a nasty car accident.

00:15:19.217 --> 00:15:19.759
Ah-ha...

00:15:19.968 --> 00:15:25.140
But a regular operator could
never do that. ln other words, he'<i>s...</i>

00:15:26.391 --> 00:15:29.811
He's good. Outrageously good.

00:15:32.522 --> 00:15:34.524
Anyway, this means we won?

00:15:34.732 --> 00:15:35.567
Yeah.

00:15:35.775 --> 00:15:38.027
That's right! lt's unbelievable!

00:15:39.028 --> 00:15:40.989
We won!

00:15:43.950 --> 00:15:46.578
That was something else, l tell you!

00:15:46.786 --> 00:15:48.580
I knew he'd do it.

00:15:48.788 --> 00:15:51.499
You were saying he had no chance.

00:15:55.837 --> 00:15:59.632
If nothing else, thanks. You bailed us out.

00:15:59.841 --> 00:16:01.509
No problem. But more importantly...

00:16:01.718 --> 00:16:03.178
Wh-What?

00:16:03.386 --> 00:16:05.930
Can l keep working for you?

00:16:06.139 --> 00:16:07.974
If l can secure money for
a hotel and three meals a day,

00:16:08.183 --> 00:16:10.185
l 'm willing to strike a deal.

00:16:13.563 --> 00:16:16.024
Of course. By all means.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.071
Man, that was thrilling!

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.448
What a relief it was!

00:16:23.656 --> 00:16:26.201
Hey, chief! You get any good photos?

00:16:26.409 --> 00:16:29.829
I was so engrossed in the match, l forgot.

00:16:31.164 --> 00:16:33.333
Hey, l ' ll have another beer!

00:16:33.541 --> 00:16:34.834
Enjoying yourself?

00:16:35.043 --> 00:16:35.877
Affirmative.

00:16:36.085 --> 00:16:37.086
Me, too!

00:16:37.295 --> 00:16:39.214
--Two more beers!
--Everyone's cutting loose.

00:16:39.422 --> 00:16:42.091
Looks like they've forgotten all about Rick.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:44.093
That's better than being depressed.

00:16:44.302 --> 00:16:45.678
I guess.

00:16:45.887 --> 00:16:49.474
On that note, where did
you learn to operate an AS?

00:16:49.682 --> 00:16:53.394
With a Savage l stole from the enemy
in the Helmajistan civil war.

00:16:53.603 --> 00:16:55.063
That was six or seven years ago.

00:16:55.271 --> 00:16:57.065
You mean you were a guerrilla?

00:16:57.273 --> 00:17:00.610
And you 're about the same age as <i>me.</i>

00:17:00.818 --> 00:17:02.529
Weren 't you a child back then?

00:17:05.323 --> 00:17:07.867
Sorry. That was too nosy.

00:17:08.076 --> 00:17:10.954
No. Can l ask you something, too?

00:17:11.162 --> 00:17:12.372
What?

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.875
Where did you get that Savage?
lt's an old mech,

00:17:16.084 --> 00:17:18.044
but it's not something
a private citizen can buy.

00:17:18.253 --> 00:17:22.173
I found it. On the outskirts of my old village.

00:17:22.382 --> 00:17:25.468
You know how this country
was at war until three years ago?

00:17:25.677 --> 00:17:26.594
Yeah.

00:17:26.803 --> 00:17:29.806
My village burned down,
and my family got split up.

00:17:30.014 --> 00:17:31.432
Everybody died.

00:17:31.641 --> 00:17:34.269
The Savage belonged to
the ones who attacked the village.

00:17:34.477 --> 00:17:36.646
It ran out of fuel and they abandoned it.

00:17:36.854 --> 00:17:41.276
I had it hidden in the mountains,
thinking l 'd sell it off someday.

00:17:41.484 --> 00:17:44.821
But there's something l want to do.
l don 't have money, though.

00:17:45.029 --> 00:17:49.075
I tried dancing downstairs at
a few places around here, but no dice.

00:17:49.284 --> 00:17:52.120
And so, we have the arena.

00:17:52.328 --> 00:17:53.621
You can earn that much there?

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:57.917
We' re talking huge sums.
lf you advance to Class A and keep winning,

00:17:58.126 --> 00:18:00.044
you can live as luxuriously as you want.

00:18:00.253 --> 00:18:03.298
Well, not that l have
any interest in a luxury condo.

00:18:03.506 --> 00:18:06.134
Then what will you do with your earnings?

00:18:07.427 --> 00:18:09.053
I want to rebuild the village.

00:18:09.262 --> 00:18:12.640
With the money l make here,
l 'll restore the ruined fields

00:18:12.849 --> 00:18:17.270
and fix the roads and bridges.
l 'll also restart the school.

00:18:17.478 --> 00:18:18.396
School?

00:18:18.605 --> 00:18:22.400
Right. A small school building
where l used to attend.

00:18:22.609 --> 00:18:26.321
The teacher wound up dead,
but it was a good school.

00:18:26.529 --> 00:18:28.323
School, huh...

00:18:31.993 --> 00:18:33.453
You two!

00:18:33.661 --> 00:18:37.832
What're you making those sour faces for?!
Get over here and drink!

00:18:38.041 --> 00:18:40.501
Wow, you 've totally blended in now.

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:44.881
Well, yeah! l 'm, you know, the sponsor!
The most important guy!

00:18:45.089 --> 00:18:46.257
That's patronizing!

00:18:46.466 --> 00:18:49.344
Anyway, let's live it up!

00:18:50.136 --> 00:18:52.513
Good work today. You guys get home safe.

00:18:52.722 --> 00:18:54.182
Yep!

00:19:00.688 --> 00:19:02.315
Is your hotel that way?

00:19:02.523 --> 00:19:04.609
--Yeah.
--Here's where we part, then.

00:19:04.817 --> 00:19:07.153
Ten AM tomorrow,
in front of the hangar. Okay?

00:19:07.362 --> 00:19:08.196
Understood.

00:19:08.404 --> 00:19:10.239
Okay, good night.

00:19:33.429 --> 00:19:35.723
It's dangerous to walk down
the street alone at night!

00:19:35.932 --> 00:19:36.599
Dao!

00:19:36.808 --> 00:19:40.520
You really took care of me today.
l 'm here to thank you!

00:19:40.728 --> 00:19:41.813
Right?!

00:19:42.689 --> 00:19:47.193
Th-The loser gets his revenge, huh?
You 're rotten to the core.

00:19:47.402 --> 00:19:51.114
Now hear this!
Every time you use a crude word,

00:19:51.322 --> 00:19:53.741
l 'll hit you! Be careful.

00:19:53.950 --> 00:19:55.535
You piece of shit!

00:19:56.452 --> 00:20:00.707
You don 't understand the rules!
Well, l 'm gonna pound them into you.

00:20:00.915 --> 00:20:02.166
Stop it...!

00:20:02.375 --> 00:20:05.336
Speaking of which, that little brat you hired?

00:20:05.545 --> 00:20:07.004
I took care of him, too.

00:20:07.213 --> 00:20:10.299
You mean Sousuke? You monster!

00:20:11.509 --> 00:20:15.096
I told you, crude words aren 't allowed.

00:20:15.304 --> 00:20:16.389
Didn 't l?!

00:20:17.515 --> 00:20:18.808
He's Sousuke, huh?

00:20:19.016 --> 00:20:22.854
Right now, he's probably dead--kissin' the
ground in some neighborhood back alley.

00:20:23.062 --> 00:20:25.148
Such a pity!

00:20:25.356 --> 00:20:27.024
You 're talking about me?

00:20:28.526 --> 00:20:32.780
Dao, was it? Your henchman
is asleep, kissing the ground.

00:20:34.365 --> 00:20:36.784
Let her go. l 'd rather avoid trouble.

00:20:39.996 --> 00:20:41.664
Ah, hell.

00:20:41.873 --> 00:20:43.499
Die!

00:20:51.257 --> 00:20:53.760
Don 't move! Respiratory tract,
nerves, carotid artery.

00:20:53.968 --> 00:20:55.470
I missed them all with the stab!

00:20:55.678 --> 00:20:58.264
But if my hand moves just a little...

00:21:01.726 --> 00:21:04.645
Never lay a finger on her again. Swear it!

00:21:04.854 --> 00:21:08.149
L... l-l swear!

00:21:08.357 --> 00:21:08.983
And you guys?

00:21:09.192 --> 00:21:10.651
Y-Yeah, we swear.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:11.944
You win!

00:21:12.153 --> 00:21:13.905
Let Dao go.

00:21:16.699 --> 00:21:17.784
Go.

00:21:26.209 --> 00:21:27.168
I 'm sorry.

00:21:27.376 --> 00:21:29.295
Wh-Why apologize?

00:21:29.504 --> 00:21:32.089
It might have been best
if l 'd killed him after all.

00:21:32.298 --> 00:21:35.218
He's probably not the sort
to back off, even after that.

00:21:35.426 --> 00:21:38.888
L-l 'm not so sure.
He really was scared, wasn't he?

00:21:39.096 --> 00:21:41.098
I hope so. But more importantly...

00:21:41.307 --> 00:21:42.141
What?

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:43.601
What do we do now?

00:21:43.810 --> 00:21:47.814
They probably know where
we're both staying. lt's dangerous.

00:21:49.273 --> 00:21:53.444
We'd be better off in some high-class hotel
that caters to foreigners.

00:21:53.653 --> 00:21:55.238
I know just the place!

00:22:03.287 --> 00:22:06.249
My head 's pounding...

00:22:06.457 --> 00:22:08.668
l drank too much...

00:22:18.719 --> 00:22:20.137
What's going on?

00:22:20.346 --> 00:22:22.849
Did <i>l...</i> With an underage...?

00:22:23.057 --> 00:22:24.600
Wait, huh?

00:22:27.562 --> 00:22:29.730
I can 't eat another <i>bite...</i>

00:22:32.024 --> 00:22:34.485
What kind of sleep-talking is <i>tha!</i>

00:24:05.993 --> 00:24:07.453
" Episode 6
Rotten Repose "

00:24:07.453 --> 00:24:09.789
